**user**:
> How do I change the shapefile for a leaflet in Shiny? I call leaflet(spdf) initially, with the spatial data frame for the shapefile, but later I want to show a different shapefile.
**assistant**:
> To dynamically update the shapefile displayed in a Leaflet map within a Shiny app, you can use a reactive expression combined with the `leafletProxy` function. Here's a step-by-step approach:
> 
> 1. **Load and Initialize the Leaflet Map**: In your server code, create an initial Leaflet map using `leafletOutput` and use `leaflet` to define the initial view.
> 
> 2. **Make Shapefile Reactive**: Use a reactive expression to hold the shapefile spatial data. This allows you to update the spatial data based on user inputs or other logic in your app.
> 
> 3. **Use `leafletProxy` to Update the Map**: When you want to change the shapefile, use `leafletProxy` to add new spatial data to the existing map. You can use functions like `clearShapes` or `clearGroup` to remove old shapes if needed.
> 
> Here's a minimal example to illustrate these steps:
> 
> ```r
> library(shiny)
> library(leaflet)
> library(rgdal)  # Assuming you're using rgdal to read shapefiles
> 
> ui <- fluidPage(
>   leafletOutput("map"),
>   actionButton("switch", "Switch Shapefile")
> )
> 
> server <- function(input, output, session) {
>   # Initial shapefile
>   shapefile1 <- readOGR(dsn = "path/to/shapefile1", layer = "layer_name1")
>   shapefile2 <- readOGR(dsn = "path/to/shapefile2", layer = "layer_name2")
>   
>   # Reactive value to store current shapefile
>   current_shape <- reactiveVal(shapefile1)
>   
>   # Render initial map
>   output$map <- renderLeaflet({
>     leaflet() %>%
>       addTiles() %>%
>       addPolygons(data = current_shape())
>   })
>   
>   # Observe button click to switch shapefile
>   observeEvent(input$switch, {
>     # Toggle shapefile
>     if (identical(current_shape(), shapefile1)) {
>       current_shape(shapefile2)
>     } else {
>       current_shape(shapefile1)
>     }
>     
>     # Update the map with new shapefile
>     leafletProxy("map") %>%
>       clearShapes() %>%  # Or clearGroup() if your polygons are in a group
>       addPolygons(data = current_shape())
>   })
> }
> 
> shinyApp(ui, server)
> ```
> 
> In this example, when the button is clicked, the shapefile being shown on the map is toggled between `shapefile1` and `shapefile2`. You can expand this logic to switch between any number of shapefiles or add more complex interactions. Make sure you handle the clearing of previous polygons or shapes properly to avoid rendering them on top of each other.
